;;
;; The sticky carry enters the sweeps by stratum. :c is sticky and reached
;; by the ticket's first event, so every later read carries it. :d waits on
;; :c and negates :a, which sits in an earlier stratum (depth 0 against
;; :d's 1), as the stratification lint requires. Were the carry seeded into
;; the first snapshot, :d would see :c reached before :a had entered and
;; fire beside :a, reached with its own guard false. The carry joins in
;; :c's stratum instead, :a is in the snapshot when :d is judged, and :d
;; stays out.
{:process/id :sticky-carry
 :process/version 1
 :process/guard-vocab 2
 :lint {:runbooks :off}

 :process/stages
 [{:stage/id :a :guards []}
  {:stage/id :b :guards []}
  {:stage/id :c :stage/sticky? true :guards []}
  {:stage/id :d :after [:c] :guards [[:not [:stage-reached :a]]]}]}
